Translation patch: EdwardsPoint::to_montgomery_batch (src/edwards.rs)

Change: `eds.iter().map(..).collect()` and `eds.iter().zip(denominators.iter())` become index `while` loops
pushing into a `Vec::with_capacity(n)`.

Why: Aeneas fails on borrows threaded through iterator adaptors over slices
(`iter`/`iter_mut` combined with `zip`/`rev`/`map`/`collect`/`fold` closures):
"Internal error" in InterpBorrowsCore.ml.

Behaviour: identical. Each iterator pass becomes a `while` loop over an index
`0..n` (forwards) or `n..0` (backwards, via `k -= 1` at the top of the loop)
visiting the same elements in the same order and performing the same
operations on them; `inputs[i]` / `scratch[i]` replace the zipped references.
The indexing cannot panic and `zip` never truncates: the index stays below
`n = inputs.len()` and the zipped slices always have length `n`. They are either
built with length `n` in this function, or (for `internal_invert_batch` /
`invert_batch_internal`, private functions) every caller passes a `scratch` of the
same length as `inputs`, which is also `debug_assert`ed.

Remove this patch when Aeneas translates the original code: delete the file,
run ./scripts/aeneas-translate.sh, and check it succeeds.

diff --git a/curve25519-dalek/src/edwards.rs b/curve25519-dalek/src/edwards.rs
index 2a75012..5b2a9ef 100644
--- a/curve25519-dalek/src/edwards.rs
+++ b/curve25519-dalek/src/edwards.rs
@@ -592,23 +592,31 @@ pub fn to_montgomery(&self) -> MontgomeryPoint {
     /// Converts a large batch of points to Edwards at once. This has the same
     /// behavior on identity elements as [`Self::to_montgomery`].
     #[cfg(feature = "alloc")]
     pub fn to_montgomery_batch(eds: &[Self]) -> Vec<MontgomeryPoint> {
         // Do the same thing as the above function. u = (1+y)/(1-y) = (Z+Y)/(Z-Y).
         // We will do this in a batch, ie compute (Z-Y) for all the input
         // points, then invert them all at once
 
         // Compute the denominators in a batch
-        let mut denominators = eds.iter().map(|p| &p.Z - &p.Y).collect::<Vec<_>>();
+        let n = eds.len();
+        let mut denominators = Vec::with_capacity(n);
+        let mut i = 0;
+        while i < n {
+            denominators.push(&eds[i].Z - &eds[i].Y);
+            i += 1;
+        }
         FieldElement::invert_batch_alloc(&mut denominators);
 
         // Now compute the Montgomery u coordinate for every point
-        let mut ret = Vec::with_capacity(eds.len());
-        for (ed, d) in eds.iter().zip(denominators.iter()) {
-            let u = &(&ed.Z + &ed.Y) * d;
+        let mut ret = Vec::with_capacity(n);
+        let mut i = 0;
+        while i < n {
+            let u = &(&eds[i].Z + &eds[i].Y) * &denominators[i];
             ret.push(MontgomeryPoint(u.to_bytes()));
+            i += 1;
         }
 
         ret
     }
 
     /// Compress this point to `CompressedEdwardsY` format.
